# Real SSE frames, receiver death, reconnect and duplicate stop

## Goal

Observe a Property over Server-Sent Events from a disposable server in this
notebook: real frames arrive through the runtime subscription envelope, a
dead receiver ends the subscription, a permanent subscription reconnects
after the stream closes and resolves a fresh credential for the new
handshake, a duplicate stop is harmless, and an event over the byte bound
ends the session instead of growing.

## Prerequisites

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:wotex_lab, "~> 0.1.0"},
  {:req, "~> 0.7.4"},
  {:bandit, "~> 1.12"},
  {:plug, "~> 1.18"}
])
```

The requirements above are published-artifact requirements. At the time this
notebook was written none of the `wotex*` packages is published on Hex; the
notebook is verified against the workspace source cohort recorded in
`priv/provenance/source-cohort.json` by `test/wotex/lab/cookbook_test.exs`,
which evaluates every Elixir cell below in order (skipping this install
cell). `Mix.install/1` never points at a Git checkout.

## Package and consumer ownership

| Concern | Owner | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Subscription process, envelope, receiver monitoring, restart semantics | `wotex_runtime` (package-implements) | `Wotex.Runtime.Subscription`, `ConsumedThing.observation_child_spec/4` |
| SSE handshake validation and event values | `wotex_binding_http` (package-implements) | `Wotex.Binding.HTTP.SSE.Event` |
| Bounded incremental SSE parsing and the linked stream session | `wotex_lab` (consumer-implements `Wotex.Binding.HTTP.Client`) | `Adapters.HTTP.SSE.Parser`, `SSE.Session` |
| Reconnect | host decision: a permanent child spec restarts and re-enters credential resolution | `restart: :permanent` below |
| Supervision of subscriptions | consumer (`wotex_lab` instance `:sessions` role) | `Wotex.Lab.start_child/3` |
| The stream server | this notebook | per-run `http_handler` function plug |

## Run

```elixir
alias Wotex.Binding.HTTP
alias Wotex.Lab
alias Wotex.Lab.Adapters.HTTP.ReqClient
alias Wotex.Lab.Adapters.Runtime.StaticRef
alias Wotex.Lab.Telemetry
alias Wotex.Runtime.{ConsumedThing, Context, Error, Subscription}
alias Wotex.ThingDescription

telemetry_id = "cookbook-observe-sse-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"

events =
  for component <- Telemetry.components(),
      operation <- Telemetry.operations(),
      event <- [:start, :stop, :exception, :measurement],
      do: [:wotex, :lab, component, operation, event]

:ok = :telemetry.attach_many(telemetry_id, events, &Telemetry.forward/4, self())
```

The server keeps one scripted stream at a time: it reports each handshake
(with the Authorization header it saw) to this notebook, then sends whatever
chunks the notebook pushes until told to close. Its handler and recursive
stream loop are per-run functions, not a module recompiled on every evaluation.

```elixir
owner = self()
{:ok, controller} = Agent.start_link(fn -> %{owner: owner, stream: nil} end)

import Plug.Conn

finish_stream = fn conn, controller ->
  try do
    Agent.update(controller, &Map.put(&1, :stream, nil))
    conn
  catch
    :exit, _controller_gone -> conn
  end
end

stream_loop = fn loop, conn, controller ->
  receive do
    {:chunk, data} ->
      case chunk(conn, data) do
        {:ok, conn} -> loop.(loop, conn, controller)
        {:error, _reason} -> finish_stream.(conn, controller)
      end

    :close ->
      finish_stream.(conn, controller)
  after
    10_000 -> finish_stream.(conn, controller)
  end
end

http_handler = fn conn, controller ->
  case {conn.method, conn.request_path} do
    {"GET", "/properties/temperature/observe"} ->
      handler = self()
      Agent.update(controller, &Map.put(&1, :stream, handler))
      owner = Agent.get(controller, & &1.owner)
      send(owner, {:stream_opened, get_req_header(conn, "authorization")})

      conn =
        conn
        |> put_resp_content_type("text/event-stream")
        |> put_resp_header("cache-control", "no-cache")
        |> send_chunked(200)

      stream_loop.(stream_loop, conn, controller)

    _other ->
      send_resp(conn, 404, "")
  end
end

{:ok, server} =
  Bandit.start_link(
    plug: {http_handler, controller},
    ip: {127, 0, 0, 1},
    port: 0,
    startup_log: false
  )

{:ok, {_ip, port}} = ThousandIsland.listener_info(server)

stream = fn ->
  Enum.find_value(1..200, fn _attempt ->
    Agent.get(controller, & &1.stream) || (Process.sleep(5) && nil)
  end)
end

push = fn chunk -> send(stream.(), {:chunk, chunk}) end
close_stream = fn -> send(stream.(), :close) end
```

The observe Form requires a bearer credential so a reconnect visibly
resolves a new one: the lookup hands out `token-1`, `token-2`, ... in order.

```elixir
fixture = Application.app_dir(:wotex_lab, "priv/fixtures/http/thing-description.json")
{:ok, fixture_td} = fixture |> File.read!() |> ThingDescription.parse()
document = ThingDescription.to_map(fixture_td)

[read_form, observe_form] = document["properties"]["temperature"]["forms"]
secured_observe = Map.put(observe_form, "security", ["bearer_sc"])

{:ok, td} =
  document
  |> Map.put("base", "http://127.0.0.1:#{port}/")
  |> put_in(["properties", "temperature", "forms"], [read_form, secured_observe])
  |> ThingDescription.from_map()

{:ok, counter} = Agent.start_link(fn -> 0 end)

credentials =
  {StaticRef,
   %{
     references: %{"bearer_sc" => "vault://room/sse"},
     lookup: fn "vault://room/sse" ->
       {:ok, {:bearer, "token-#{Agent.get_and_update(counter, &{&1 + 1, &1 + 1})}"}}
     end
   }}

{:ok, profile} = HTTP.profile()
{:ok, config} = HTTP.config(client: {ReqClient, %{}}, max_event_bytes: 64)

{:ok, consumed} =
  ConsumedThing.new(td,
    profiles: [profile],
    transports: %{profile.id => HTTP.transport(config)},
    credentials: credentials
  )

{:ok, lab} = Lab.start_link(id: "observe-sse", max_children: 8)
context = Context.new!(request_id: "sse-observe")

observe = fn id, receiver, restart ->
  {:ok, spec} =
    ConsumedThing.observation_child_spec(consumed, "temperature", context,
      id: id,
      receiver: receiver,
      restart: restart
    )

  {:ok, pid} = Lab.start_child(lab, :sessions, spec)
  pid
end
```

Real frames: an event with `id` and `retry` fields, a comment keep-alive that
decodes to nothing, and a multi-line `data` that is not valid JSON and is
reported as an undecodable frame without ending the stream.

```elixir
first = observe.(:sse_first, self(), :temporary)

handshake_one =
  receive do
    {:stream_opened, auth} -> auth
  after
    2_000 -> :no_handshake
  end

push.("event: temperature\r\nid: 41\r\nretry: 250\r\ndata: 22.5\r\n\r\n")

frame =
  receive do
    {:wotex_runtime, :sse_first, {:ok, value, meta}} -> {value, meta}
  after
    2_000 -> :no_frame
  end

push.(": keep-alive\n\n")

keepalive =
  receive do
    {:wotex_runtime, :sse_first, message} -> message
  after
    100 -> :nothing_delivered
  end

push.("data: 1\ndata: 2\n\n")

invalid =
  receive do
    {:wotex_runtime, :sse_first, {:error, %Error{} = error}} -> error.code
  after
    2_000 -> :no_error
  end

{handshake_one, frame, keepalive, invalid, Process.alive?(first)}
```

Duplicate stop: the first stop closes the session and connection; a second
stop finds no process and returns Runtime's typed `subscription_not_running`
error without exiting the caller.

```elixir
:ok = Subscription.stop(first)
duplicate_stop = Subscription.stop(first)

{Process.alive?(first), duplicate_stop}
```

Receiver death: the subscription monitors its receiver and shuts down with
`:receiver_down` when it dies.

```elixir
receiver = spawn(fn -> receive do: (:quit -> :ok) end)
second = observe.(:sse_receiver, receiver, :temporary)
monitor = Process.monitor(second)

_handshake_two =
  receive do
    {:stream_opened, auth} -> auth
  after
    2_000 -> :no_handshake
  end

send(receiver, :quit)

receiver_down =
  receive do
    {:DOWN, ^monitor, :process, ^second, reason} -> reason
  after
    2_000 -> :still_alive
  end
```

Reconnect: a permanent child is restarted by the instance after the server
closes the stream, and the new handshake carries a freshly resolved token.

```elixir
durable = observe.(:sse_durable, self(), :permanent)

handshake_three =
  receive do
    {:stream_opened, auth} -> auth
  after
    2_000 -> :no_handshake
  end

close_stream.()

lost =
  receive do
    {:wotex_runtime, :sse_durable, {:status, status}} -> status
  after
    2_000 -> :no_status
  end

handshake_four =
  receive do
    {:stream_opened, auth} -> auth
  after
    2_000 -> :no_reconnect
  end

push.("data: 19.0\n\n")

after_reconnect =
  receive do
    {:wotex_runtime, :sse_durable, {:ok, value, _meta}} -> value
  after
    2_000 -> :no_frame
  end

{handshake_three, lost, handshake_four, after_reconnect, Process.alive?(durable)}
```

## Deliberate breakage

An event larger than `max_event_bytes` ends the session: the parser refuses
to buffer it, the session exits and the subscription reports the transport
as down.

```elixir
close_stream.()

_replacement =
  receive do
    {:stream_opened, _auth} -> :ok
  after
    2_000 -> :no_reconnect
  end

big = observe.(:sse_big, self(), :temporary)
big_monitor = Process.monitor(big)

_handshake_five =
  receive do
    {:stream_opened, _auth} -> :ok
  after
    2_000 -> :no_handshake
  end

push.("data: " <> String.duplicate("9", 100) <> "\n\n")

oversized =
  receive do
    {:DOWN, ^big_monitor, :process, ^big, reason} -> reason
  after
    2_000 -> :still_alive
  end
```

```elixir
:ok = Supervisor.stop(lab)
:ok = ThousandIsland.stop(server)
:ok = Agent.stop(controller)
:ok = Agent.stop(counter)
```

## Safe telemetry

Subscription spans carry the method and profile; the parser emits byte
counts as measurements. Tokens and frame contents never appear.

```elixir
drain = fn drain ->
  receive do
    {:wotex_lab_telemetry, event, measurements, metadata} ->
      [{event, measurements, metadata} | drain.(drain)]
  after
    0 -> []
  end
end

spans = drain.(drain)
:telemetry.detach(telemetry_id)

parse_bytes =
  for {[:wotex, :lab, :sse, :parse, :measurement], %{bytes: bytes}, _metadata} <- spans, do: bytes

text = inspect(spans)
labels_safe? = parse_bytes != [] and not (text =~ "token-") and not (text =~ "22.5")
{Enum.sum(parse_bytes), labels_safe?}
```

## Expected output

| Check | Expectation |
| --- | --- |
| `frame-decoded` | `22.5` arrives with `event`, `id` `"41"` and `retry` `250` |
| `keepalive-ignored` | A comment line delivers nothing |
| `invalid-frame-reported` | Multi-line non-JSON data is `:undecodable_frame` and the subscription stays alive |
| `receiver-death-stops` | The subscription exits with `{:shutdown, :receiver_down}` |
| `reconnect-fresh-credential` | After `:transport_down` a new handshake carries a different bearer token |
| `duplicate-stop-safe` | The second stop is a typed not-running error |
| `oversized-event-ends-session` | A 100-byte event over a 64-byte bound ends with `{:shutdown, :transport_down}` |

```elixir
%{
  "frame-decoded" => match?({22.5, %{event: "temperature", id: "41", retry: 250}}, frame),
  "keepalive-ignored" => keepalive == :nothing_delivered,
  "invalid-frame-reported" => invalid == :undecodable_frame,
  "receiver-death-stops" => receiver_down == {:shutdown, :receiver_down},
  "reconnect-fresh-credential" =>
    lost == :transport_down and after_reconnect == 19.0 and
      match?(["Bearer token-" <> _], handshake_three) and
      match?(["Bearer token-" <> _], handshake_four) and handshake_three != handshake_four,
  "duplicate-stop-safe" =>
    match?({:error, %Error{code: :subscription_not_running}}, duplicate_stop),
  "oversized-event-ends-session" => oversized == {:shutdown, :transport_down} and labels_safe?
}
```

## Public seam

`http.client` — `Wotex.Binding.HTTP.Client.subscribe/4` and `close/2`
(consumer-implements; the Lab session parses SSE and links to the
subscription). `runtime.credentials` for the per-handshake token.

## Spec and completion IDs

* Lab: WLB.04 (`WLB-C04`, `WLB-C08`).
* Upstream consumer evidence: `RT-C02`, `RT-C04`, `WBH-C02`, `WBH-C03`,
  `WBH-C04`.

## Replacement adapter

A replacement client's `subscribe/4` must open the stream, validate the
handshake status and media type, send each SSE event to the owner as
`{:wotex_transport_frame, %Wotex.Binding.HTTP.SSE.Event{}}`, and exit with a
`:shutdown` reason when the stream ends or a bound is exceeded. Do not
reconnect inside the client: a restart policy on the subscription child spec
is the reconnect, and it re-enters `Wotex.Runtime.Credentials.resolve/4`.
